  "description": "Erection of hip-to-gable and rear dormer roof extension with installation of 2nos. front rooflights. Conversion of single dwelling house into 2nos. self-contained flats. Provision of refuse and cycle storage",
  "development_type": "Minor dwellings",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "The development to which this permission relates shall be carried out in accordance with the materials specified on the approved plans and on the submitted application form unless otherwise agreed in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance on completion of the development, in accordance with Policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies CS8 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the landscaping details shown on the approved plans. The approved landscaping shall be implemented in the first planting season following substantial completion of the development and shall thereafter be maintained for a period of five years. Any trees or plants which die, are removed or become seriously damaged or diseased within this period shall be replaced in the next planting season.\r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance of the development and to enhance the character of the area in accordance with Policies CS8 and DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012) and Policy G6 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "The development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved Fire Safety Strategy and thereafter maintained. \r\rReason: In the interests of fire safety and to ensure the safety of all building users, in accordance with Policy D12 of the London Plan 2021.\r",
    "Prior to beneficial occupation of the development to which this permission relates, a close boarded timber fence, 1.8m in height as measured from ground level adjacent to each panel, shall be erected along the adjoining external amenity areas of the site. All fencing shall accord with BS 1722-5:2006 and shall be retained for a period of at least five years.\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy D3 of the London Plan 2021 and policy DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.\r",
    "The cycle parking facilities shown on the approved plans shall be provided prior to first occupation of the development and retained thereafter for cycle parking purposes.\r\rReason: To ensure adequate provision for sustainable transport in accordance with Policy T5 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM8 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012).",
    "The refuse and recycling storage facilities shown on the approved plans shall be provided prior to first occupation of the development and retained thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory waste management and to safeguard the appearance of the development in accordance with Policies CS8 and DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012) and Policy SI 7 of the London Plan (2021).",
    "The vehicle parking space shown on the approved plans shall be retained and kept available for parking purposes for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To ensure adequate off-street parking provision and to safeguard highway safety in accordance with Policy T6.1 of the London Plan (2021) and Policies DM8 and DM9 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012).",
    "Prior to the commencement of development, a Construction Management Plan (CMP) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The CMP shall include details of:\r\rconstruction vehicle routing\rloading and unloading arrangements\rcontractor parking\rhours of construction\rmeasures to minimise impacts on the public highway\r\rThe development shall thereafter be carried out in accordance with the approved CMP.\r\rReason: To safeguard highway safety and the free flow of traffic during construction in accordance with Policies T4 and T7 of the London Plan (2021), Policy DM9 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012), and the National Planning Policy Framework (2024)."
  ],
